 "珍": "نَادِر (Very uncommon; scarce.)  [rare]\nمثال: あの珍本をどうやって手に入れたのですか。\n→ How did you come by those rare books? / غَرِيب, عَجِيب (Not normal; odd, unusual, surprising, out of the ordinary, often with a negative) / أَجْنَبِيّ, غَرِيب (Unfamiliar, not yet part of one's experience.)  [strange]",
 "珍か": "نَادِر (Very uncommon; scarce.)  [rare]",
 "珍しい": "نَادِر (Very uncommon; scarce.)  [rare]\nمثال: これは珍しい種類の魚です。\n→ This is a strange kind of fish. / جَدِيد (recently made or created) / حَدِيث (recently made or created) / جديد (recently made or created) / جَديد (recently made or created) / جديد (recently made or created) / جديد (recently made or created)  [new] / غَرَامَة (A fee levied as punishment for breaking the law.) / غَرَّمَ (To issue a fine as punishment to (someone).)  [fine]",
 "珍中の珍": "تَمّ أَسْوَد (Cygnus atratus, a swan with black plumage and a red bill which is endemic to Aus)  [black swan]",
 "珍事": "[strange incident ; unusual occurrence] / حَادِث (A collision or crash of a vehicle, aircraft, or other form of transportation tha) / مُصَادَفَة, صُدْفَة (Any chance event.) / صُدْفَة, صِدْفَة (Chance; random chance.)  [accident]\nesp. 椿事",
 "珍奇": "غَرِيب, عَجِيب (Not normal; odd, unusual, surprising, out of the ordinary, often with a negative) / أَجْنَبِيّ, غَرِيب (Unfamiliar, not yet part of one's experience.)  [strange]",
