 "甘露水": "شَرَاب, قَطْر (Any thick liquid that has a high sugar content and which is added to or poured o)  [syrup]",
 "甚だ": "جِدًّا (To a great extent or degree.)  [very]\nمثال: 彼はやたらに故事来歴に詳しいけれど、それが人生の役に立っているのかはなはだ疑問だね。\n→ He has a great storehouse of knowledge about historical details but I seriously doubt that's of any use in life.",
 "甚だしい": "الْأُقْصَى, الْأَبْعَد (Of a place, the most remote, farthest or outermost.) / شَدِيد (In the greatest or highest degree; intense.) / غَيْر اِعْتِيَادِيّ (Excessive, or far beyond the norm.) / خَطِير (Drastic, or of great severity.) / مُتَطَرِّف (Of sports, difficult or dangerous; performed in a hazardous environment.) / أَخِير (Ultimate, final or last.)  [extreme]\nمثال: あんなことを彼女に言うなんて非常識も甚だしい。\n→ It's quite absurd of you to tell her that sort of thing.",
 "甚大": "ضَخْم, هَائِل (Extremely large; greatly exceeding the common size, extent, etc.)  [enormous]\nمثال: その会社は甚大な被害を被った。\n→ The company suffered big losses.",
 "甚振る": "عَذَاب (Any extreme pain, anguish or misery, either physical or mental.) / عَذَّبَ (To cause severe suffering to (stronger than to vex but weaker than to torture.))  [to torment] / [to extort ; to shake down]",
 "甜菜": "شَمَنْدَر اَلسُّكَّر (A type of beet whose root contains a high concentration of sucrose.)  [sugar beet (Beta vulgaris)]",
 "生": "صَافٍ, اَلصَّافِي (Free of flaws or imperfections; unsullied.) / صَافٍ, اَلصَّافِي (Free of foreign material or pollutants.)  [pure]",
 "生々": "دَجِر (Full of life; energetic, vivacious.)  [lively] / [being born and raised ; growing up]",
 "生々しい": "طَازَج, طَازَة (Newly produced or obtained; recent.) / عَذْب (Without salt; not saline.)  [fresh]\nمثال: その出来事は今でも私の記憶に生々しく残っている。\n→ The event still remains vivid in my memory. / طَازَج, طَازَة (Newly produced or obtained; recent.) / عَذْب (Without salt; not saline.)  [fresh (blood, scar, etc.)]",
 "生々世々": "أَبَد (Existence without end, infinite time.) / أبَدِيَّة (A period of time which extends infinitely far into the future.)  [eternity]",
 "生い立ち": "تَنْمِيَة, نُمُو (An increase in size, number, value, or strength.)  [growth] / تَرْبِيَة (The traits acquired during one's childhood training) / تَرْبِيَة (The raising or training of a child.)  [upbringing]",
 "生い立つ": "نَمَى ((intransitive) to become bigger) / كَبُرَ ((intransitive) to become bigger)  [to grow]",
 "生い茂る": "اِزْدَهَرَ, أَهَلَّ (To increase in wealth or success; to prosper, be profitable.)  [to thrive]\nمثال: その木々は葉が生い茂っている。\n→ The trees have exuberant foliage.",
 "生う": "نَمَى ((intransitive) to become bigger) / كَبُرَ ((intransitive) to become bigger)  [to grow (of plants)]",
 "生えでる": "نَبْتَة (A new growth of or on a plant, whether from seed or other parts.)  [to sprout]",
 "生える": "نَمَى ((intransitive) to become bigger) / كَبُرَ ((intransitive) to become bigger)  [to grow]\nمثال: おたまじゃくしは大きくなるにつれ、尻尾が消えて足が生えはじめる。\n→ As a tadpole grows, the tail disappears and legs begin to form. / جَرَحَ (To incise, to cut into the surface of something.) / قَصَّ (To remove (text, a picture, etc.) and place in memory in order to paste at a lat)  [to cut (teeth)]\nمثال: この子は今歯が生えかけているところです。\n→ This child is teething now.",
 "生え出る": "نَبْتَة (A new growth of or on a plant, whether from seed or other parts.)  [to sprout]",
 "生え抜き": "[native-born ; trueborn]\nمثال: 彼は生え抜きの外交官として一生の大部分を送ってきた。\n→ He has spent most of his time as a career diplomat. / مُنْذُ البِدَايَة (From the very beginning.)  [(belonging) from the start (to a group, organization, etc.)]",
 "生かじり": "لَحَنَ (To speak (a language or words) with only a superficial knowledge of it.)  [smattering] / [dabbler ; dilettante] / [dipping into]",
 "生かす": "[to make (the best) use of ; to put to good use]\nمثال: 彼はわずかな収入を精一杯活かした。\n→ He made the best of his small income. / [to let live ; to keep alive]\nمثال: 自分も生き、他人も生かせ。\n→ Live and let live. / أَحْيَا (transitive: to bring back to life)  [to revive]\nمثال: 心停止の患者を応急処置で生かした。\n→ We used emergency measures to revive the cardiac arrest patient. / اِسْتَعَادَ (to bring back to a previous condition or state)  [to restore (a deleted passage; in proofreading)]",
 "生き": "حَيّ (Having life; alive.) / مَعِيشَة, مَعَاش (Financial means; a means of maintaining life; livelihood) / حَيَاة, طَرِيقَة فِي حَيَاة (A style of life.)  [living] / [freshness ; liveliness] / [situation in which a group of stones cannot be captured because it contains two or more gaps] / [stet (proofreading) ; leave as-is]\nusually イキ",
 "生きかえる": "أَحْيَا (transitive: to bring back to life)  [to revive]\nمثال: 雨が降ればこの木は生き返るでしょう。\n→ The rain will revive this tree.",
 "生きがい": "سَبَب الْوُجُود (A reason for being; the claimed reason for the existence of something or someone)  [raison d'être]\nمثال: 今や彼には何の生きがいもない。\n→ Now he has nothing to live for.",
 "生きがいい": "طَازَج, طَازَة (Newly produced or obtained; recent.) / عَذْب (Without salt; not saline.)  [fresh (e.g. fish)] / دَجِر (Full of life; energetic, vivacious.)  [lively]",
 "生きが良い": "طَازَج, طَازَة (Newly produced or obtained; recent.) / عَذْب (Without salt; not saline.)  [fresh (e.g. fish)] / دَجِر (Full of life; energetic, vivacious.)  [lively]",
 "生きざま": "حَيَاة, طَرِيقَة فِي حَيَاة (A style of living that reflects the attitudes of a person or group.)  [way of life]\nمثال: 生きざまの立派な人は死にざまも立派である。\n→ They die well that live well.",
 "生きた": "حَيِيَ, عَاشَ (To be alive; to have life.) / يَنْجُو (To survive; to persevere; to continue.) / حَيّ (Having life; that is alive.) / مُباشِر (Being broadcast (“on the air”), as it happens.)  [live]",
 "生きた化石": "حفرية حية (Any species discovered first as a fossil and believed extinct, but which is late)  [living fossil]",
 "生きている化石": "حفرية حية (Any species discovered first as a fossil and believed extinct, but which is late)  [living fossil]",
 "生きながらえる": "نَجَا (Of a person, to continue to live; to remain alive.) / نَجَا (Of an object or concept, to continue to exist.) / نَجَا (To live past (a life-threatening event))  [to survive]\nمثال: 彼は妻の死後、何年も生きながらえていた。\n→ After his wife died, he lived for quite a few more years.",
 "生きぬく": "نَجَا (Of a person, to continue to live; to remain alive.) / نَجَا (Of an object or concept, to continue to exist.) / نَجَا (To live past (a life-threatening event))  [to survive]\nمثال: その日その日を生き抜くのがやっとだ。\n→ I'm just living from day to day.",
 "生きのいい": "طَازَج, طَازَة (Newly produced or obtained; recent.) / عَذْب (Without salt; not saline.)  [fresh (e.g. fish)] / دَجِر (Full of life; energetic, vivacious.)  [lively]",
 "生きの良い": "طَازَج, طَازَة (Newly produced or obtained; recent.) / عَذْب (Without salt; not saline.)  [fresh (e.g. fish)] / دَجِر (Full of life; energetic, vivacious.)  [lively]",
 "生きる": "حَيِيَ, عَاشَ (To be alive; to have life.) / يَنْجُو (To survive; to persevere; to continue.) / حَيّ (Having life; that is alive.) / مُباشِر (Being broadcast (“on the air”), as it happens.)  [to live] / اِرْتَزَقَ (To earn enough income to support oneself and, if applicable, one's family.)  [to make a living] / وَظِيفَة (What something does or is used for.) / مَهَمَّة (A professional or official position.) / دَالَّة, تَابِع (A relation in which each element of the domain is associated with exactly one el) / وَظِيفَة, دَالَّة (A routine that receives zero or more arguments and may return a result.)  [to function]\nمثال: この本はまだ版権が生きている。\n→ This book is still copyrighted. / [to come to life ; to be enlivened]",
 "生きる道": "حَيَاة, طَرِيقَة فِي حَيَاة (A style of living that reflects the attitudes of a person or group.)  [way of life]",
 "生き存える": "نَجَا (Of a person, to continue to live; to remain alive.) / نَجَا (Of an object or concept, to continue to exist.) / نَجَا (To live past (a life-threatening event))  [to survive]\nمثال: 彼は妻の死後、何年も生きながらえていた。\n→ After his wife died, he lived for quite a few more years.",
 "生き延びる": "نَجَا (Of a person, to continue to live; to remain alive.) / نَجَا (Of an object or concept, to continue to exist.) / نَجَا (To live past (a life-threatening event))  [to survive]\nمثال: 自然がそうした生き延びるための手段を与えているのである。\n→ Nature provides them with the means of survival.",
 "生き抜く": "نَجَا (Of a person, to continue to live; to remain alive.) / نَجَا (Of an object or concept, to continue to exist.) / نَجَا (To live past (a life-threatening event))  [to survive]\nمثال: その日その日を生き抜くのがやっとだ。\n→ I'm just living from day to day.",
 "生き方": "حَيَاة, طَرِيقَة فِي حَيَاة (A style of living that reflects the attitudes of a person or group.)  [way of life]\nمثال: 人の死に方は、その人の生き方を見ればわかる。\n→ As a man lives, so shall he die.",
 "生き様": "حَيَاة, طَرِيقَة فِي حَيَاة (A style of living that reflects the attitudes of a person or group.)  [way of life]\nمثال: 生きざまの立派な人は死にざまも立派である。\n→ They die well that live well.",
 "生き残り": "[survival]\nمثال: 会社は生き残りを賭けて奮闘している。\n→ The company is struggling for survival. / أَثَر (That which remains; that which is left after loss or decay; a remaining portion.) / ذَخِيرَة (A part of the body of a saint, or an ancient religious object, kept for venerati)  [relic]",
 "生き残る": "نَجَا (Of a person, to continue to live; to remain alive.) / نَجَا (Of an object or concept, to continue to exist.) / نَجَا (To live past (a life-threatening event))  [to survive]\nمثال: 彼が生き残ったということは注目すべきことだ。\n→ That he survived was remarkable.",
 "生き永らえる": "نَجَا (Of a person, to continue to live; to remain alive.) / نَجَا (Of an object or concept, to continue to exist.) / نَجَا (To live past (a life-threatening event))  [to survive]\nمثال: 彼は妻の死後、何年も生きながらえていた。\n→ After his wife died, he lived for quite a few more years.",
 "生き物": "حَيَوَان (A multicellular organism of the kingdom Animalia that is usually mobile, with ce) / حَيَوَان (Any member of the kingdom Animalia other than a human.) / حَيَوَان, وَحْش (A person who behaves wildly; a bestial, brutal, brutish, cruel, or inhuman perso)  [animal]\nمثال: 王を得た麒麟もまた寿命を持たない生き物だが、この病ばかりは治癒の方法がない。\n→ A qilin with a king too has no limit on its lifespan, but this illness alone admits of no remedy.",
