 "生き返る": "أَحْيَا (transitive: to bring back to life)  [to revive]\nمثال: 雨が降ればこの木は生き返るでしょう。\n→ The rain will revive this tree.",
 "生き長らえる": "نَجَا (Of a person, to continue to live; to remain alive.) / نَجَا (Of an object or concept, to continue to exist.) / نَجَا (To live past (a life-threatening event))  [to survive]\nمثال: 彼は妻の死後、何年も生きながらえていた。\n→ After his wife died, he lived for quite a few more years.",
 "生く": "حَيِيَ, عَاشَ (To be alive; to have life.) / يَنْجُو (To survive; to persevere; to continue.) / حَيّ (Having life; that is alive.) / مُباشِر (Being broadcast (“on the air”), as it happens.)  [to live] / [to bring to life]",
 "生ける": "رَتَّبَ (To set up; to organize; to put into an orderly sequence or arrangement.)  [to arrange (flowers)]\nمثال: 彼女は花を生けるのが好きです。\n→ She likes to arrange flowers. / حَيّ (Having life; alive.) / مَعِيشَة, مَعَاش (Financial means; a means of maintaining life; livelihood) / حَيَاة, طَرِيقَة فِي حَيَاة (A style of life.)  [living]",
 "生け垣": "وَشِيع, سِيَاج نَبَاتِيّ (A thicket of bushes or other shrubbery, especially one planted as a fence betwee)  [hedge]\nمثال: 猫は生け垣を通り抜けた。\n→ The cat got through the hedge.",
 "生け簀": "حَوْض سَمَك (A container, usually made out of glass or acrylic, specifically designed for hol)  [fish tank]",
 "生け花": "إِيكِيبَانَا (The Japanese art of flower arrangement.)  [ikebana]\nمثال: 生け花は日本では伝統的な芸道である。\n→ Flower arrangement is a traditional art in Japan. / [fresh flower ; natural flower]",
 "生け贄": "تَضْحِيَة, قُرْبَان (A human being or an animal, or a physical object or immaterial thing (see etymol) / ضَحَّى ((transitive) to offer (a human being or an animal, or an obj)  [(living) sacrifice] / ضَحِيَّة (one who is harmed) / أُضْحِيَّة (a living being slain and offered as a sacrifice)  [victim]\nمثال: タランチュラはそのいけにえを素早く捕まえた。\n→ The tarantula seized its victim very quickly.",
 "生け込む": "رَتَّبَ (To set up; to organize; to put into an orderly sequence or arrangement.)  [to arrange (e.g. flowers)]",
 "生じる": "أَنْتَجَ, صَنَعَ (To bring forth, to yield, make, manufacture, or otherwise generate.)  [to produce]\nمثال: 事故は不注意から生じる。\n→ Accidents arise from carelessness. / نَهَضَ (To spring up; to come into action, being, or notice; to become operative, sensib)  [to arise]",
 "生じろい": "بَاهِت, شَاحِب (Light in color.) / لَوْح (A wooden stake; a picket.) / تَخْم, حَدّ (Limits, bounds (especially before of).)  [pale]",
 "生す": "نَمَى ((intransitive) to become bigger) / كَبُرَ ((intransitive) to become bigger)  [to grow (of moss, grass, etc.)]",
 "生ずる": "أَنْتَجَ, صَنَعَ (To bring forth, to yield, make, manufacture, or otherwise generate.)  [to produce]\n生ずる is more literary than 生じる\nمثال: この構成において、三角形の代わりに長方形を用いても類似の困難が生ずる。\n→ We encounter similar difficulties when we substitute rectangles for triangles in this configuration. / نَهَضَ (To spring up; to come into action, being, or notice; to become operative, sensib)  [to arise]",
 "生っちょろい": "سَاذَج (Lacking worldly experience, wisdom, or judgement; unsophisticated.)  [naive]",
 "生っちろい": "بَاهِت, شَاحِب (Light in color.) / لَوْح (A wooden stake; a picket.) / تَخْم, حَدّ (Limits, bounds (especially before of).)  [pale]",
 "生っ白い": "بَاهِت, شَاحِب (Light in color.) / لَوْح (A wooden stake; a picket.) / تَخْم, حَدّ (Limits, bounds (especially before of).)  [pale]",
 "生っ粋": "صَافٍ, اَلصَّافِي (Free of flaws or imperfections; unsullied.) / صَافٍ, اَلصَّافِي (Free of foreign material or pollutants.)  [pure]\nمثال: 彼は生粋のパリっ子です。\n→ He is a Parisian born and bred.",
 "生つば": "لُعَاب, رِيق (A clear, slightly alkaline liquid secreted into the mouth by the salivary glands)  [saliva (in one's mouth)]",
