 "直す": "أَصْلَحَ (To restore to good working order, fix, or improve damaged condition; to mend; to) / تَصْلِيح (act of repairing something) / إِصْلَاح (act of repairing something) / تَرْمِيم (act of repairing something) / مَرَمَّة (act of repairing something)  [to repair]\nمثال: いまそれを直そうったって無駄だ。\n→ It's no use trying to fix it now. / تَغَيَّرَƒ (To become something different.) / غَيَّرَ (To make something into something else.) / تَغْيِير, تَبْدِيل (The process or result of becoming different.) / فَكَّة (Small denominations of money given in exchange for a larger denomination.) / بَاقٍ (Balance of money returned from the sum paid after deducting the price of a purch) / تَغْيِير (A transfer between vehicles.)  [to change] / [to put back ; to put away]\nمثال: その本をなおしなさい。\n→ Put the book back where you found it. / شِفَاء (A method, device or medication that restores good health.) / شَفَى (To restore to health.)  [to cure]\nusu. written as 治す",
