 "移す": "حَوَّلَ (To move or pass from one place, person or thing to another.) / اِنْتِقَال (act)  [to transfer (to a different place, group, etc.)]\nمثال: 委員会は別のホールに会場を移した。\n→ The committee adjourned to another hall. / [to move to the next stage (of a plan, etc.)]\nمثال: 知っていることと行動に移すことは別だ。\n→ To know is one thing, and to do is another. / [to divert (one's attention) to ; to focus on (something different)] / أَنْفَقَ, صَرَفَ (To pay out (money).) / قَضَى (To consume, to use up (time).)  [to spend (time)]",
 "移り": "تَحَوُّل, نَقِل (The process of change from one form, state, style or place to another.)  [transitioning] / [gift placed inside a container when returning it]",
 "移りゆく": "تَغَيَّرَƒ (To become something different.) / غَيَّرَ (To make something into something else.) / تَغْيِير, تَبْدِيل (The process or result of becoming different.) / فَكَّة (Small denominations of money given in exchange for a larger denomination.) / بَاقٍ (Balance of money returned from the sum paid after deducting the price of a purch) / تَغْيِير (A transfer between vehicles.)  [to change]",
 "移り住む": "حَرُكَ, تَحَرَّكَ (To change place or posture; to go, in any manner, from one place or position to ) / اِنْتَقَلَ, تَحَلْحَلَ (To change residence, for example from one house, town, or state, to another; to )  [to move (to another area, country, etc.)]\nمثال: カールがドイツに移り住むと聞いた時には驚いた。\n→ It took me by surprise to hear that Carl was moving to Germany.",
 "移り変り": "تَغَيَّرَƒ (To become something different.) / غَيَّرَ (To make something into something else.) / تَغْيِير, تَبْدِيل (The process or result of becoming different.) / فَكَّة (Small denominations of money given in exchange for a larger denomination.) / بَاقٍ (Balance of money returned from the sum paid after deducting the price of a purch) / تَغْيِير (A transfer between vehicles.)  [change (e.g. season)]\nمثال: 青年期は移り変わりの時期と見られている。\n→ Adolescence is viewed as time of transition.",
 "移り変る": "تَغَيَّرَƒ (To become something different.) / غَيَّرَ (To make something into something else.) / تَغْيِير, تَبْدِيل (The process or result of becoming different.) / فَكَّة (Small denominations of money given in exchange for a larger denomination.) / بَاقٍ (Balance of money returned from the sum paid after deducting the price of a purch) / تَغْيِير (A transfer between vehicles.)  [to change (with time, the ages, the seasons, etc.)]",
 "移り変わり": "تَغَيَّرَƒ (To become something different.) / غَيَّرَ (To make something into something else.) / تَغْيِير, تَبْدِيل (The process or result of becoming different.) / فَكَّة (Small denominations of money given in exchange for a larger denomination.) / بَاقٍ (Balance of money returned from the sum paid after deducting the price of a purch) / تَغْيِير (A transfer between vehicles.)  [change (e.g. season)]\nمثال: 青年期は移り変わりの時期と見られている。\n→ Adolescence is viewed as time of transition.",
 "移り変わる": "تَغَيَّرَƒ (To become something different.) / غَيَّرَ (To make something into something else.) / تَغْيِير, تَبْدِيل (The process or result of becoming different.) / فَكَّة (Small denominations of money given in exchange for a larger denomination.) / بَاقٍ (Balance of money returned from the sum paid after deducting the price of a purch) / تَغْيِير (A transfer between vehicles.)  [to change (with time, the ages, the seasons, etc.)]",
 "移り気": "مُتَقَلِّب (Impulsive and unpredictable; determined by chance, impulse, or whim.)  [capricious]\nمثال: 彼女の移り気にはみんな当惑している。\n→ We are all bewildered by her inconstancy.",
 "移り行く": "تَغَيَّرَƒ (To become something different.) / غَيَّرَ (To make something into something else.) / تَغْيِير, تَبْدِيل (The process or result of becoming different.) / فَكَّة (Small denominations of money given in exchange for a larger denomination.) / بَاقٍ (Balance of money returned from the sum paid after deducting the price of a purch) / تَغْيِير (A transfer between vehicles.)  [to change]",
 "移る": "حَرُكَ, تَحَرَّكَ (To change place or posture; to go, in any manner, from one place or position to ) / اِنْتَقَلَ, تَحَلْحَلَ (To change residence, for example from one house, town, or state, to another; to )  [to move (to another place or state)]\nocc. used transitively\nمثال: ハイジャック犯達は飛行機の後部に移った。\n→ The hijackers moved to the rear of the plane. / نَشَرَ (To disperse, to scatter or distribute over a given area.) / نَشَرَ (To disseminate; to cause to proliferate, to make (something) widely known or pre) / اِنْتِشَار (The act of spreading.)  [to spread (of a fire, smell, etc.)]\nocc. written 伝染る or 感染る in ref. to infection\nمثال: 枝葉末節の議論はもうそろそろ止めにして、本筋の話に移りませんか。\n→ Why don't we stop arguing over these piddling matters and get to the issues at hand? / حَرُكَ, تَحَرَّكَ (To change place or posture; to go, in any manner, from one place or position to ) / اِنْتَقَلَ, تَحَلْحَلَ (To change residence, for example from one house, town, or state, to another; to )  [to move (e.g. of one's focus)] / [to be permeated (by a color or scent) ; to seep into]",
 "移ろい": "تَغَيَّرَƒ (To become something different.) / غَيَّرَ (To make something into something else.) / تَغْيِير, تَبْدِيل (The process or result of becoming different.) / فَكَّة (Small denominations of money given in exchange for a larger denomination.) / بَاقٍ (Balance of money returned from the sum paid after deducting the price of a purch) / تَغْيِير (A transfer between vehicles.)  [change]\nمثال: 靜子が季節の移ろいを詩に綴りました。\n→ Shizuko composed a poem about the change of the seasons. / تَقْلِيعَة (A phenomenon that becomes popular for a very short time.)  [fading]",
 "移ろう": "تَغَيَّرَƒ (To become something different.) / غَيَّرَ (To make something into something else.) / تَغْيِير, تَبْدِيل (The process or result of becoming different.) / فَكَّة (Small denominations of money given in exchange for a larger denomination.) / بَاقٍ (Balance of money returned from the sum paid after deducting the price of a purch) / تَغْيِير (A transfer between vehicles.)  [to change (with the passage of time)] / رَفَضَ (To choose not to do something; refuse, forbear, refrain.)  [to decline]",
 "移住": "هِجْرَة (An instance of moving to live in another place for a while.)  [migration]\nمثال: 一家は１８３０年頃故国のドイツからシカゴに移住した。\n→ The family moved from their native Germany to Chicago around the year 1830.",
 "移住民": "مُهَاجِر, مُهَاجِرَة (A non-native person who comes to a country from another country to permanently s)  [immigrant]",
 "移住者": "مُهَاجِر, مُهَاجِرَة (Someone who leaves a country to settle in a new country.)  [emigrant]\nمثال: 移住者の部落が野蛮人によって征服され、移住者の希望も生活も土壇場にきた時、長い歳月をかけての不幸とのたたかいに終止符がうたれた。\n→ Years of resistance to misfortune ended when the settlers' village was overcome by the savages and their hopes and lives came to the bitter…",
 "移入": "مُقَدَّمَة (The act or process of introducing.) / تَعْرِيف (A means, such as a personal letter, of presenting one person to another.) / مُقَدَّمَة, مَدْخَل (An initial section of a book or article, which introduces the subject material.)  [introduction (from outside)] / نَقَلَ (To carry or bear from one place to another; to remove; to convey.) / نَقْل (An act of transporting; conveyance.)  [transporting] / [putting in (e.g. one's feelings into a work)]",
 "移出": "نَقَلَ (To carry or bear from one place to another; to remove; to convey.) / نَقْل (An act of transporting; conveyance.)  [transporting]",
 "移動": "حَرَكَة (Physical motion between points in space.) / حَرَكَة (A trend in various fields or social categories, a group of people with a common )  [movement]\nمثال: 平和な丘や田園地帯から、通りがあり群衆がいる忙しい世界へと移動するのである。\n→ They are moving from the peaceful hills and the countryside to the busy world of streets and crowds. / مُنْتَقِل (capable of being moved) / مُتَنَقِّل (capable of being moved)  [mobile]",
 "移動式": "مُنْتَقِل (capable of being moved) / مُتَنَقِّل (capable of being moved)  [mobile]",
 "移動性": "هِجْرَة (An instance of moving to live in another place for a while.)  [migration] / مُنْتَقِل (capable of being moved) / مُتَنَقِّل (capable of being moved)  [mobile]",
 "移動電話": "جَوَّال, هَاتِف مَحْمُول (A portable (handheld) telephone that connects with the cellular telephone networ)  [mobile phone]",
 "移受換": "حَوَّلَ (To move or pass from one place, person or thing to another.) / اِنْتِقَال (act)  [transfer (of a pension)]",
 "移替": "تَغَيَّرَƒ (To become something different.) / غَيَّرَ (To make something into something else.) / تَغْيِير, تَبْدِيل (The process or result of becoming different.) / فَكَّة (Small denominations of money given in exchange for a larger denomination.) / بَاقٍ (Balance of money returned from the sum paid after deducting the price of a purch) / تَغْيِير (A transfer between vehicles.)  [changing (person in charge, etc.)]",
 "移染": "[dye migration ; dye transfer] / اِمْتِصَاص (The act or process of absorbing or of being absorbed as,)  [absorption (of one chemical by another)]",
 "移植": "زَرَعَ, شَتَلَ (To uproot (a growing plant), and plant it in another place.) / زَرَعَ (To transfer (tissue or an organ) from one body to another, or from one part of a) / زَرْع (An operation (procedure) in which tissue or an organ is transplanted: an instanc)  [transplanting (a plant)]\nمثال: アメリカの文化はヨーロッパから移植されたものだ。\n→ The American culture had been transplanted from Europe. / زَرَعَ, شَتَلَ (To uproot (a growing plant), and plant it in another place.) / زَرَعَ (To transfer (tissue or an organ) from one body to another, or from one part of a) / زَرْع (An operation (procedure) in which tissue or an organ is transplanted: an instanc)  [transplant] / [embryo transfer ; embryo transplant] / مِينَاء, مينا (A place on the coast at which ships can shelter, or dock to load and unload carg) / مَنْفَذ (A logical or physical construct in and from which data are transferred. Computer) / كَيَّفَ, غَيَّرَ (To adapt, modify, or recode to work on a different platform.)  [porting (software)]",
 "移植片": "طُعْم (A portion of living tissue used in the operation of autoplasty.)  [graft]",
 "移民": "هِجْرَة, مُهَاجَرَة (The act of immigrating; the passing or coming into a country of which one is not)  [immigration]\nمثال: 合衆国は長い間「るつぼ」として知られているが、それは国民のほとんどが移民の子孫だからである。\n→ The United States has long been known as a \"melting pot\" because most of its people are descended from immigrants. / مُهَاجِر, مُهَاجِرَة (A non-native person who comes to a country from another country to permanently s)  [immigrant]\nمثال: ドイツの首相は移民問題に悩まされています。\n→ The German Chancellor is plagued by immigration problems.",
 "移民団": "مُهَاجِر, مُهَاجِرَة (Someone who leaves a country to settle in a new country.)  [emigrants]",
 "移監": "حَوَّلَ (To move or pass from one place, person or thing to another.) / اِنْتِقَال (act)  [transfer (of a prisoner to another institution of confinement)]",
 "移籍": "حَوَّلَ (To move or pass from one place, person or thing to another.) / اِنْتِقَال (act)  [transfer (of one's name into another family register)] / حَوَّلَ (To move or pass from one place, person or thing to another.) / اِنْتِقَال (act)  [transfer (to another team, company, etc.)]",
 "移行": "تَحَوُّل, نَقِل (The process of change from one form, state, style or place to another.)  [transition]\nمثال: 英国は、１９７１年にその貨幣制度を１０進法に移行させた。\n→ In 1971 the United Kingdom changed its currency to the decimal system. / حَوَّلَ (To move or pass from one place, person or thing to another.) / اِنْتِقَال (act)  [transfer (of powers, weight, etc.)]",
 "移設": "مُتَحَرِّك (That moves or move.) / مُؤَثِّر (Causing or evoking deep emotions.)  [moving (to a different site)]",
 "移譲": "حَوَّلَ (To move or pass from one place, person or thing to another.) / اِنْتِقَال (act)  [transfer]",
 "移転": "مُتَحَرِّك (That moves or move.) / مُؤَثِّر (Causing or evoking deep emotions.)  [moving]\nمثال: ４月１日、南洋フーズ株式会社は横浜の新社屋に移転します。\n→ On April 1, Nanyo Foods Co. Ltd. will move to its new building in Yokohama. / حَوَّلَ (To move or pass from one place, person or thing to another.) / اِنْتِقَال (act)  [transfer (of deeds, property, etc.)]",
